{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793671511550,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"id":"prt_19f273de8001ijNScWZ8tWqv7A","messageID":"msg_19f27267b0016aIlPWFwKbfYuY","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","snapshot":"32b4d478ebaf10e95bd6b084a004445291213aba","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1793671519222,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"id":"prt_19f27545d001Zg1bL3ePedjpjq","messageID":"msg_19f27267b0016aIlPWFwKbfYuY","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","type":"text","text":"The drawer did not close on its own in staging: in all four combinations it stayed open at 2s, at 5s and after a click on empty drawer space. I changed nothing and made no third commit.\n\n**Setup:** staging at `127.0.0.1:4396` was still running the final Round 3 binary (hash starts `2b64573c7366e7ca`, the same as `target/release/openfang`), so no restart was needed. Clicks were real input events: a touch tap on the phone width, a mouse click on desktop. Phone is 390×844; desktop is a 1440-wide window.\n\n**Sampled states:**\n\n| Combination | Before click | Right after click | +2s | +5s | After clicking empty drawer area |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| phone-light | closed, at −360px | open, slide-in starting | open, at 0 | open, at 0 | open, at 0 (and at +2s) |\n| phone-dark | closed, at −360px | open, slide-in starting | open, at 0 | open, at 0 | open, at 0 (and at +2s) |\n| desk-light | closed, at −378px | open, slide-in starting | open, at 0 | open, at 0 | open, at 0 (and at +2s) |\n| desk-dark | closed, at −378px | open, slide-in starting | open, at 0 | open, at 0 | open, at 0 (and at +2s) |\n\n- **Right after the click:** the `open` class was already set, but the card still read at its closed position because the 0.32s slide-in had only just begun. By 2s it was fully in place and stayed there.\n- **Click target:** I confirmed the spot was the drawer's empty scroll area (`sd-body`), not a button or link, before clicking. On phone it was the space below Sign out; on desktop, a point 60px below the Owner block.\n- **No drag state was ever applied** at any sample.\n- **One false alarm:** my first desktop attempt picked a spot that turned out to be on the \"Report a bug\" row. That click closed the drawer because the row opens a page, which closes the drawer by design. I moved the click to empty space and re-ran.\n\nThe captures are in `~/openfang-build/round3-shots/` as `remains-open-<config>-t0.png` and `-t5.png`, eight files in total.\n\n**Verdict:** the \"does not open and stay open\" behaviour did not reproduce on the Round 3 staging binary in any of the four combinations. Your report is from the live Round 2 build, so this doesn't show what caused it on the bench phone. This check also can't stand in for the actual phone app with a real finger, so the phone remains the final proof once Round 3 is deployed.\n\nSeparately, `stax-ux` has moved on since my two commits: someone merged a Canvas R1 branch on top as `217ceb4`. The staging binary was built before that merge, so it contains only Round 3.","time":{"start":1793671517277,"end":1793671519215}}}
